sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, one Swamp run, Ansible phases for idempotent Node state (rule 22). docs/reference/node-provisioning.md.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: node:role:remove
  %% kind: node.role_remove
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane P icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant P as Fleet Nodes<br/>hub · DNS
  CLI->>GW: node:role:remove<br/>NODE ROLE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:role:remove NODE ROLE`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> <role> [--force] [--purge-data] [--offline] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node and the role to remove
  %%> - `--force` is consent; without a terminal, `--purge-data` and `--offline` need it
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to the target Node
  %%> - the target is an active, managed Linux Node, and the role is not `vpn`, `router` or `swamp`
  %%> - the role is `active` or `failed`; a `provisioning` or `removing` role is refused until its claim is stale
  %%> - `app-dev` and `app-prod` have no Route targets, `ingress` no public Routes, and `analytics` no tracking hosts
  %%> - one add, converge or remove Operation per Node (`operation.target_busy`); a second removal after the first finished finds no such role (`http.404`)
  %%> Then:
  %%> - the Gateway reads the recorded state of the assignment and picks one of the two paths below
  alt the role never touched the Node
    Note over GW: Delete the role
    %%> When:
    %%> - the Gateway recorded that the assignment failed before its first step that changes the Node, and no later run started
    %%> - an assignment from before that record, and one with any later run, takes the withdrawal below
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the assignment and its settings are deleted; no run starts and nothing else is checked on the Node
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID, already succeeded
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the task ID, at once; the task has ended `succeeded`
  else the role may have changed the Node
    Note over GW: Mark removing
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the assignment is recorded as `removing`, and a task is recorded with the full intent
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>node-role-remove
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the task ID, at once
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
    SW->>N: Reach the Node<br/>SSH argv
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - probes the Node with its approved identity
    %%> - an unreachable Node without `--offline` fails the run here (`node.removal_incomplete`); a reachable Node gets ordinary cleanup even with `--offline`
    opt CI role is being removed
      SW->>N: Require drained CI<br/>SSH argv · native assert
      %%> Why:
      %%> - the run fails here, `node.removal_incomplete`, while CI guests still run on the Node, and the rerun after they are drained succeeds
    end
    opt the last role leaves
      SW->>N: Keep public SSH access<br/>SSH argv
      %%> Why first:
      %%> - removing the last role restores public recovery SSH before anything else is torn down, so the Node stays reachable
    end
    SW->>P: Withdraw from the fleet<br/>PHP · sites · DNS · Metrics
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - withdraws the role's PHP pools, Caddy sites, private DNS records, Metrics exporter entries and role certificates on the other Nodes
    %%> - an `--offline` removal of an unreachable Node does only the work on other Nodes
    opt Node reachable
      SW->>N: Remove the role<br/>Ansible phase: remove
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - stops the role's services and removes its files, configuration, containers, firewall rules and certificates
      %%> Retained:
      %%> - role data, CI resources, release data and container volumes, unless `--purge-data`
      opt --purge-data
        SW->>N: Remove role data<br/>Ansible phase: purge
        %%> What it does:
        %%> - for `metrics`, the Prometheus and Grafana volumes and the stored credentials; for `websocket`, the Reverb checkout; for `ci-runner`, the Incus project, network and ACL
      end
      SW->>N: Check the removal<br/>Ansible phase: check
      %%> Why:
      %%> - the one end check: the removed files, directories and containers are gone
    end
    alt every step passes
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Delete the role
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the assignment is deleted
    else a step fails
      N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or mismatch
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      Note over GW: Mark the role failed
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the assignment stays, `failed` at `remove:STEP`, with the step's own error code
      %%> - a failed public SSH restore leaves the Node reachable, and the rerun restores it
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - finished steps stay; there is no rollback
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the same command again: each removal step is safe to repeat over what a failed convergence left
    end
    opt run completed or failed
      SW->>SW: Remove the run folder<br/>private run files
    end
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
